00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:02.750
--You should be grateful.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.040
--Um, sorry about this.
We thought you knew we were coming.
--You should be grateful.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.050
--Um, sorry about this.
We thought you knew we were coming.
--Come on. You're my pal.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:13.510
This is the first ever dorado
she's caught! Come on, now!

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:18.310
Next time, you need
to contact me beforehand.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.560
You got it!

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:23.810
All right. How do you
want to eat this thing?

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:26.690
How do you usually eat dorados?

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:28.530
They have a really mild taste,

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:32.280
so we usually deep fry them
or sauté them with butter.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:36.620
It's so hard to choose!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:40.080
We've got a real pro here,
so why don't we eat it raw?

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:43.330
You can shut your mouth now.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:47.000
Well, it is summer,
so we can try a carpaccio.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.290
Fancy!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:51.130
Yes, please.

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:55.430
Huh? Are dorados this drab?

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.600
I could've sworn they looked more vivid.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.850
When dorados are swimming,
they have a silver body

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:05.020
with gradients of blue and green...

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:08.400
But when they get worked up,
they shine yellow.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:12.190
And once they die,
they turn a darker color, like this.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:16.570
Oh, I see. I figured we were just dealing
with a different species of dorados.

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:20.200
Their colors change so much
you would think that, huh?

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.540
Are you disinfecting it?

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.620
Yeah. When eating this raw,

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:29.000
you need to thoroughly wash
your cutting board and knife,

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.590
or change them out completely.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.670
Yeah, because getting
food poisoning is scary!

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.970
I dunno. I think the person
who brought said scary fish

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.090
into my shop suddenly is way scarier.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:44.180
Once we chop it up,
we chill the flesh in the fridge.

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.390
Do you fish, Ms. Miyano?

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:50.520
Hm... I've done a little
bait fishing at least.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:52.980
Miyano actually hunts!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:54.190
She's a hunter?

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:59.410
I hunt pheasants and wild ducks.
I usually prepare anything I catch here.

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.990
That's so cool!

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.540
Uh-huh.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:07.670
Hunting season starts in November,
so I can't serve any of that today.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.420
November, huh? That's a long ways off.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.210
Here's the pheasant skin of one
I caught earlier this year.

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.180
I've seen those at Koi's shop!

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:21.220
It's really pretty.
What exactly do you use this for?

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:25.020
I give them to one of my coworkers.
They make accessories with them.

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.890
Um... Would you consider
selling them to my shop?

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.230
And Koi's entered business mode.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:34.650
This is really interesting.

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:41.280
Fishing season is basically
from March to September.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.450
Ah, so it's the opposite
of hunting season.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:49.750
Maybe people back in the day
would fish when it was warm

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:53.750
and hunt animals and eat
their meat when it got cold.

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:59.800
Then use their pelts to keep warm
as they waited for spring.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:05.640
Maybe people used to live
alongside the seasons like that.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:09.690
Er, sorry. I was just fantasizing.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.270
I'm sure there were
people like that, Hiyori!

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:14.980
That's so exciting to think about!

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.650
Yeah.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:26.410
Okay, it should be pretty chilled by now.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:29.660
We're going to season them
with salt and <i>arabiki </i>pepper.

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:34.460
To add some colors, we'll throw in
some sliced tomatoes and baby leaves.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.630
Then throw on some olive oil
and balsamic vinegar.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:43.680
And the dorado carpaccio is complete!

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:45.100
It looks so good.

00:19:45.100 --> 00:19:46.720
Now, then...

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.730
Let's eat!

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.480
It's so chewy and delicious!

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.780
Miyano, get me some wine!
White wine, pronto!

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.530
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.200
Thank you for the meal.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:09.410
Thank you for everything today.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:12.670
Not a problem. Come by again sometime.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:16.540
Ms. Miyano, I hope you'll consider
selling us some pheasant skins.

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:18.710
You got it.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.800
You're not going home?

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:23.800
I'm gonna drink a little more.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.350
And I'm scared to go home.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.720
Did you flake out of work again?

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:31.270
But you know...

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:37.520
You sure warmed up to those girls quickly.
You're always so annoyed.

00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:41.150
Have you seriously never
thought about who's annoying me?

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:45.280
But I've seen your cute side, too.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.950
I swear you never listen.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.290
This sure takes me back.

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:50.790
"Prize"

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:54.420
"Prize"

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:54.420
Split into groups of two
and come get this.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.040
"Prize"

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.040
I wish I could've paired up with Miyano.

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.130
"Prize"

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.130
I know, right? She's so cool and reliable!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:00.510
I know, right? She's so cool and reliable!

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:01.380
"Squeeze"

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.220
"Squeeze"

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.220
Like when you were scared out of your mind

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.630
"Squeeze"

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.630
when we did a test of
courage at summer camp.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:05.510
when we did a test of
courage at summer camp.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.760
That's cold!

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:10.850
Don't tell people about that.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.730
That was so good.

00:21:15.730 --> 00:21:17.690
Maybe I'll come with my family next time.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:21.530
Hey, did you show the twins the dorado?

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:24.360
Yeah, when I went back home for a sec.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.240
Wanna see a picture?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.070
Yeah!

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:32.410
Is something wrong?

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:36.540
I was happy to catch a fish
that big for the first time,

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:41.170
but it was somehow lacking a little oomph.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:46.590
Well, you did use bait fish.
And you did end up catching a baby one.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:57.480
Hiyori. Let's try again next year.

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:00.270
Next time, I'm going to
catch one by fly fishing.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:04.570
Sure.

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:09.120
Hey, wait!

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:15.620
Okay, I'm gonna raise
my skill level by then!

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:17.830
Just like you're randomly
raising your hand right now?

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.580
No!

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:20.920
Let's do our best!

00:22:20.920 --> 00:22:22.460
--Yeah!
--Yeah, you do that.

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:24.050
We will!

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:55.600
"Next Time"

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:59.270
"Next Time"

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:59.270
Ms. Miyano, when we're fly fishing,
we use English for bird names.

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:00.980
"Next Time"

00:23:59.270 --> 00:24:00.980
Oh, really? Then what's <i>kiji </i>in English?

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:02.100
"Next Time"

00:24:00.980 --> 00:24:02.100
Pheasant.

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:05.270
"Next Time"

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:05.270
It's a wonderful bird
that's useful from top to bottom.

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:07.860
"Next Time"

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:07.860
Then I'll go ahead
and cook its meat for you.

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:09.900
"Next Time"

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:09.900
You're like the best person ever.
